        },
        {
          "say": "A good question is focused, researchable, open, and linked to chemistry.",
          "write": "focused, open, chemistry"
        },
        {
          "say": "Start with to what extent, or how does this compare with that.",
          "write": "To what extent…?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Improving a question",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "First try: are bioplastics good?",
          "write": "✗ Are bioplastics good?"
        },
        {
          "say": "Too broad, good is vague, and it can be answered yes or no.",
          "write": "broad, vague, yes/no"
        },
        {
          "say": "Better: to what extent is PLA more sustainable than PET for cups?",
          "write": "✓ To what extent is PLA…?",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 300,
            "alt": "Better question",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 30,
                "y": 60,
                "w": 500,
                "h": 70,
                "fill": "red",
                "label": "Are bioplastics good?",
                "change": "remove"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 30,
                "y": 160,
                "w": 500,
                "h": 70,
                "fill": "green",
                "label": "PLA vs PET for drink cups",
                "change": "add"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "One material, one comparison, one use, and room for a judgement.",
          "write": "specific + weighed"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Primary and secondary sources",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "A primary source is the original research, like a journal article.",
          "write": "primary = the original"
        },
        {
          "say": "A secondary source retells it, like a textbook or news story.",
          "write": "secondary = the retelling",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 300,
            "alt": "Primary and secondary",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 30,
                "y": 90,
                "w": 200,
                "h": 90,
                "fill": "blue",
                "label": "journal article"
              },
              {
                "kind": "arrow",
                "x": 240,
                "y": 135,
                "x2": 320,
                "y2": 135,
                "color": "purple",
                "change": "add"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 330,
                "y": 90,
                "w": 200,
                "h": 90,
                "fill": "orange",
                "label": "news story",
                "change": "add"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 130,
                "y": 220,
                "text": "eyewitness",
                "size": 18,
                "color": "black",
                "anchor": "middle"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 430,
                "y": 220,
                "text": "retelling",
                "size": 18,
                "color": "black",
                "anchor": "middle"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "Use a mix. Search with specific terms.",
          "write": "use a mix"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Judging sources: CRAAP",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Test every source with CRAAP.",
          "write": "CRAAP test",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 300,
            "alt": "CRAAP",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
